memory-headroom guard adapted from hp_uploadprogress_guard (Hosted Power)
https://github.com/HOSTED-POWER/php_uploadprogress_guard

The following functions were taken from the component above:

  hp_mem_room()
    Checks whether there is enough memory headroom under memory_limit to
    take the next step. Returns 1 if there is room, 0 if not.

  hp_upg_filter_drop_post()
    Empties the copy of the form fields that ext/filter keeps, so that
    filter_input(), filter_has_var() and filter_input_array() don't
    return a body that has been dropped.

  hp_drop_request()
    Stops a request whose multipart body would exceed the memory headroom.
    It clears the POST and file arrays, clears the ext/filter copy, sets
    the response code to 413, and writes an entry to the error log.

